00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:23.560
EDGAR.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.040
Alright.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.600
Alright, let's get serious for a little bit.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:33.040
Deutsche Telekom, Alzheimer's Research and UCL have gotten together,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.840
to make a mobile game,

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:35.920
to fight dementia.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:36.960
That's pretty cool!

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.120
If you are not familiar with dementia,

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.120
one of the first signs of it

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.120
is loss of navigational skills.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.200
Dementia steals your memories

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.520
and the times you had with the people you love.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.840
It's...just...awful.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.360
And this game was made to conquer that.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.120
So, the game is split up in different areas

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.240
and basically you're a sea explorer,

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.760
and you need to navigate

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.400
to recover the lost memories of your father.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.840
And you follow the same journey, as he took.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.280
Ok, so here is where the game get's interesting:

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:19.400
The data from people playing this game and navigating around,

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:21.880
will be analyzed by scientists

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.680
and the more they get - the better results they will get.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:28.680
Right now, there are over 49 million people sufferng from dementia

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.680
An noone has ever survived it.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:32.880
There is no cure and it's increasing.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:37.160
There is going to be 135 million people by the year 2050.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:41.920
This game's goal is to generate the largest, crowdsource, global benchmark,

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:43.320
for how people navigate.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.920
So, if 100 000 people play this game for 2 minutes,

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:49.880
we can generate 58 years of lab research.

